<title>CANADA: Canada raw materials prices rise 0.9 pct in July.</title>
<headline>Canada raw materials prices rise 0.9 pct in July.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Canada on Wednesday issued the following economic indicators for June, base 1986=100.</p>
<p>    INDEX			 Month pct  Yr pct    July index</p>
<p>    Overall raw materials     +0.9	+3.2	135.8</p>
<p>    Mineral fuels		 +4.4     +22.3	126.3</p>
<p>    Vegetable products	  +0.2     +15.4	151.3</p>
<p>    Animals and products	+1.7	+7.5	119.7</p>
<p>    Wood			    -1.1     -11.9	206.4</p>
<p>    Ferrous materials	   +0.3	-0.7	119.8</p>
<p>    Non-ferrous metals	  -4.5     -19.4	117.3</p>
<p>    Non-metallic minerals     +0.1	+1.7	107.8</p>
<p>    Index ex mineral fuels    -0.5	-3.2	140.2</p>
<p>The raw materials price index reflects the prices paid by manufacturers for key raw materials. Unlike the industrial product price index, the raw materials price index includes goods that are not produced in Canada.</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of economists had forecast that the overall index would be unchanged.</p>
<p>(For more information, contact Statistics Canada's Client Services Unit, Prices Division at (613) 951-3350.)</p>
<p>-- Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745</p>
